# prod/config/secrets.env.example — COMMITTED template (no real secrets).
#
# prod/scripts/2-secrets.sh generates the real secrets.env (in the git-ignored
# runtime directory, mode 0600) from this shape: the three service-role
# passwords via `openssl rand`, plus an optional remote LLM API key. This
# template is the ONLY secrets.env* that is ever committed — the generated copy
# is git-ignored so a stray `git add` cannot publish a credential.
#
# Consumed by `docker compose --profile prod`: the three INFOCHAT_*_PASSWORD
# vars drive the Postgres service-role bootstrap in docker/postgres-init.sh
# (M1-378). Leave every value blank here.

# Service-role passwords (generated by 2-secrets.sh).
INFOCHAT_DB_PASSWORD=
INFOCHAT_COLLECTOR_PASSWORD=
INFOCHAT_PROVIDER_PASSWORD=

# Optional: remote LLM API key (remote-llm profile / openai-compatible provider).
# Leave blank for a local Ollama / llama.cpp setup.
INFOCHAT_LLM_API_KEY=

# Per-adapter bootstrap-admin credentials. NOT generated by 2-secrets.sh —
# prod/scripts/6-adapter.sh (wizard step 6) appends whichever of these the
# operator supplies during adapter registration. Each is optional per adapter;
# the Provider only requires that the UNION across enabled adapters is non-empty
# (§7.6.3), and 6-adapter.sh enforces that gate. The application.properties line
# for an adapter is written only when its var is set here, so an unset var pairs
# with an absent property reference and is inert.
#
# The two adapters use DIFFERENT bootstrap shapes (D50):
#  - SimpleX has no pre-seedable cryptographic sender address, so its bootstrap
#    is a single-use claim-TOKEN: a SECRET the operator chooses, written to
#    infochat.adapters.simplex.admin-token. The first DM whose body equals the
#    token becomes the bot admin. SECURITY: this is a secret — keep it out of
#    logs/VCS, and UNSET it once the first admin is claimed. Leaving it set lets a
#    leaked token re-claim admin after a /revoke-admin (the re-arm gap); unsetting
#    it closes that gap (security.md §Per-adapter admin threat profile).
#  - Signal has a stable cryptographic account id, so its bootstrap is the
#    by-ADDRESS contact id (the bot-admin ACI), written to
#    infochat.adapters.signal.admin and pre-seeded at startup.
INFOCHAT_SIMPLEX_ADMIN_TOKEN=
INFOCHAT_SIGNAL_ADMIN_CONTACT_ID=
